{
  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "For an international application filed through IP Australia, the Manual says that international fees are paid directly to WIPO, rather than to IP Australia.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part60/2/4/2/4/3~1",
          "quote": "An international application is filed with IP Australia through WIPO eFiling, accessed via the online services page."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part60/2/4/2/4/3~1",
          "quote": "The international fees are paid directly to WIPO."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The supplied passages do not establish whether an Australian domestic application requires payment to any body other than IP Australia, or provide a complete account of filing fees.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    },
    {
      "text": "Section 40 of the Act requires rejection if the trade mark cannot be represented graphically.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s40",
          "quote": "An application for the registration of a trade mark must be rejected if the trade mark cannot be represented graphically."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "As a matter of practice, the Registrar requires the representation included in the application to be a graphical representation.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/1",
          "quote": "The Registrar will, as a matter of practice, require that the representation of the trade mark that is included in the application be a graphical representation."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a mark consisting of, or containing, a colour, scent, shape, sound, aspect of packaging or other non-traditional sign, the Manual requires a concise and accurate description.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/1",
          "quote": "Each trade mark consisting of, or containing, a colour, scent, shape, sound, aspect of packaging or other non-traditional sign must also be accompanied by a concise and accurate description of the trade mark."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual says that the description is entered as an endorsement and, together with the graphical representation, helps define the scope of registration.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/1",
          "quote": "Such descriptions will be entered as endorsements and, taken together with the graphical representation, will help to define the scope of the registration."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For sound marks, the Manual calls for a recording in addition to the graphical representation, with CDs, DVDs and digital sound files identified as suitable media for supplying the actual sound.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/1",
          "quote": "In the case of sound trade marks, recordings of the sound (e.g. compact disc or digital sound file) will also be required."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4",
          "quote": "In most cases the applicant will need to file a copy of the actual sound being claimed as the trade mark. This copy should be provided on a medium which allows for easy copying, storage and replaying of the sound. CDs, DVDs and digital sound files are all suitable media."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the actual sound cannot be supplied at filing, the Manual says to send the medium incorporating it to the Office as soon as possible after filing.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4",
          "quote": "If it is not possible to provide the actual sound at the time of filing, for example, when the applicant experiences difficulties in attaching a sound file to an electronically filed application, the medium incorporating the sound should be sent to the Office as soon as possible after the application is filed."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual allows a written description of non-musical sounds as the representation, while musical notation may be most appropriate for a musical sound, depending on the mark.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/3/3",
          "quote": "The representation of the trade mark may consist of a written description of sounds if the sign is not a musical-type sound."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/3/3",
          "quote": "A sign consisting of a musical sound might be most appropriately represented in the form of musical notation, however, this will depend on the trade mark."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a three-dimensional shape mark, the Manual says an actual sample may be required; it does not state this as an automatic requirement.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/1",
          "quote": "An actual sample of the trade mark may be required for three dimensional shape trade marks."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The supplied passages do not give a complete list of additional files or technical file specifications for every type of non-traditional mark.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    }
  ],
